{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create /srv/inventory on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The directory was created, and its continued existence was directly confirmed after the reboot and verification cleanup.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b51b457879694da1","cmd-bbba6aacde1a43f9","cmd-913a83d8e1754163"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Make /srv/inventory available at /mnt/inventory through a bind mount.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct checks showed /mnt/inventory as a mounted bind view of /srv/inventory, with matching directory identities and data accessible through both paths.","evidence_ids":["cmd-65f1af84fc3546c0","cmd-bbba6aacde1a43f9","cmd-913a83d8e1754163"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Make the bind mount persistent across node restart.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before restart the mount and test data were healthy; the restart was acknowledged and bounded connection failures showed disruption; a different boot ID then appeared with the system running, mount unit active, bind mount restored, and pre-restart data intact. The persistent fstab entry remained present. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0dbbff6d45554d11","cmd-b5d5d84003c1468d","cmd-65f1af84fc3546c0","cmd-bd86c39498e54d82","cmd-4dc5978304f64ece","cmd-43f2b30e79754809","cmd-d580c6d2cb4f4525","cmd-f9195a3d8e6d43a1","cmd-bbba6aacde1a43f9","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified, and none remained or required reversion. The state-changing commands had clear roles: directory creation (cmd-b51b457879694da1), persistent fstab configuration (cmd-0dbbff6d45554d11), mount activation (cmd-15cdaebe87da431c), creation of a bounded proof marker (cmd-65f1af84fc3546c0), the required restart and persistence test (cmd-bd86c39498e54d82), and removal of the proof marker (cmd-913a83d8e1754163). Post-execution observations show no failed services, unchanged listening endpoints apart from reboot-generated PIDs, healthy package state, and only normal reboot-scoped temporary-directory replacement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b51b457879694da1","cmd-0dbbff6d45554d11","cmd-15cdaebe87da431c","cmd-65f1af84fc3546c0","cmd-bd86c39498e54d82","cmd-913a83d8e1754163","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. The source directory exists, /mnt/inventory is a functioning bind mount of it, and a directly observed reboot transition demonstrated persistent configuration, recovered mounting, and preserved cross-path data. The provider-wide restart protocol was complete for the sole managed node and agrees with the fixed lifecycle observations.","limitations":[]}
